<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madrasa al-Firdaws</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1235">1235</a>–<a href="/years/1236">1236</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a> al-Firdaws is an Islamic college and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> lodge outside the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, founded in 1235–1236 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayfa-khatun">Dayfa Khatun</a>, regent of the Ayyubid principality. Built of finely cut stone around a courtyard with a pool and an arcaded portico, it is considered one of the masterpieces of Ayyubid architecture.</p></div>
